' ==============================================================================
' @file 4-1-crisismap-architecture.puml
' @brief High-level component architecture for the Crisis Map platform.
'
' @details
' This artifact defines the principal structural components required to support 
' the Crisis Map system. The model captures the overarching software architecture, 
' encompassing the client applications, API gateways, core microservices/modules, 
' database layers, and external third-party integrations (e.g., mapping, SMS).
'
' Architectural Scope & Rationale:
' This model is explicitly scoped to the macro-architecture tier. It focuses 
' on identifying bounded contexts, system modularity, and communication protocols. 
' Code-level class structures, internal method implementations, and physical 
' network topologies are deliberately deferred to lower-level design phases.
'
' System Requirements Addressed:
' This model establishes the structural foundation of the application by defining:
' - The separation of concerns across presentation, logic, and data layers.
' - The interfaces and dependencies between core backend modules.
' - The integration points with external APIs and services.
' - The architectural constraints governing scalability and maintainability.
'
' Author(s): Vlado Sruk
' Context: Software Engineering Course
'
' AI Usage Disclosure:
' Designed by Vlado Sruk. AI-assisted revision and documentation comments were
' reviewed by the author, who is responsible for the final content.
'
' Traceability Note:
' The architectural components defined herein must strictly map to the finalized 
' repository structure and deployed services. Any architectural deviations 
' introduced during development must be retroactively updated in this model to 
' maintain evidence chain completeness from requirements to code.
'
' Diagram type: UML Component Diagram
' Abstraction:  High-level logical architecture
' Viewpoint:    Software structure and component dependencies
' ==============================================================================

@startuml

' ==============================================================================
' Diagram Layout and Style
' ==============================================================================

left to right direction

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam componentStyle rectangle

skinparam component {
    BackgroundColor #E7F1FF
    BorderColor #0D6EFD
    ArrowColor #212529
}

skinparam database {
    BackgroundColor   #FFF3CD
    BorderColor #212529
}

' ==============================================================================
' Crisis Map System Boundary and Internal Components
' ==============================================================================

rectangle "Crisis Map System" {
  component "Web client" as Web
  rectangle "Backend application" {
    component "Report API" as API
    component "Report service" as Reports
    component "Notification worker" as Notify
  }
  database "PostgreSQL" as DB
}
' ==============================================================================
' External Systems
' ==============================================================================

component "Map tile provider\n(external)" as Maps
component "Firebase Cloud Messaging\n(external)" as FCM

' ==============================================================================
' Component Dependencies and Interfaces
' ==============================================================================

Web --> API : report requests / responses
Web --> Maps : map tiles
API --> Reports : submit and retrieve reports
Reports --> DB : store and query reports
Notify --> DB : find confirmed reports\nand recipients
Notify --> FCM : send notification requests
@enduml
